You are an expert in PHP, Laravel, Livewire, Flux UI, Alpine.js, Pest, and Tailwind CSS.


1. Coding Standards
	•	Use PHP v8.4 features.
	•	Follow pint.json coding rules.
	•	Enforce strict types and array shapes via PHPStan.

2. Project Structure & Architecture
	•	Delete .gitkeep when adding a file.
	•	Stick to existing structure—no new folders.
	•	Avoid DB::; use Model::query() only.
	•	No dependency changes without approval.
	•	Use Volt routes and components ONLY for all routes and views.
	•	Use the Class-based approach for Livewire components.
	•	Use Livewire and Alpine for all frontend interactions.

2.1 Directory Conventions

app/Http/Controllers
	•	No abstract/base controllers.

app/Http/Requests
	•	Use FormRequest for validation.
	•	Name with Create, Update, Delete.

app/Actions
	•	Use Actions pattern and naming verbs.
	•	Example:

```php
public function store(CreateTodoRequest $request, CreateTodoAction $action)
{
    $user = $request->user();
    $action->handle($user, $request->validated());
}
```

app/Enums
    •	Use backed Enums for multiple options.
    •	Example:

```php
enum Status: string
{
    const Pending = 'pending';
    const Active = 'active';
    const Inactive = 'inactive';
}
```

app/Models
	•	Avoid fillable.

app/Services
    •	Use services for complex logic or third-party services.

lang
    •	No hardcoded strings.
    •	Use lang json files for all strings. (lang/en.json, lang/fr.json)
    •	Use english keys in the code.
    •	French is the default language.
    •	English is the fallback language.
    •	Translate all missing strings in the lang files.


3. Testing
	•	Use Pest PHP for all tests.
	•	Run `composer lint` after changes.
	•	Run `composer test` before finalizing.
	•	Don’t remove tests without approval.
	•	All code must be tested.
	•	Generate a {Model}Factory with each model.

3.1 Test Directory Structure
	•	Console: tests/Feature/Console
	•	Controllers: tests/Feature/Http
	•	Actions: tests/Unit/Actions
	•	Models: tests/Unit/Models
	•	Jobs: tests/Unit/Jobs

4. Styling & UI
	•	Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
	•	Use Flux UI for components.
	•	Use Alpine.js for specific frontend behaviors.

5. Task Completion Requirements
	•	Recompile assets after frontend changes.
	•	Follow all rules before marking tasks complete.

